@title Welcome to Bayside Community Pantry
@subtitle A note from Rosa Delgado, volunteer coordinator

Welcome, and thank you for joining us. We are glad you are here. This page tells you what to expect.

## Hours

We are open for distribution:

- Tuesday, 9:00 to 12:00
- Thursday, 16:00 to 19:00
- Saturday, 8:00 to 12:00

Come to as many shifts as you like.

## Your first shift

New volunteers join a 45-minute orientation at 8:00 on the first Saturday of each month, before their first shift. The next one is on 2026-11-07.

On your first shift, please:

- Arrive 15 minutes early.
- Check in with the shift lead, who wears a green apron.
- Wear closed-toe shoes.
- Leave valuables in the locker.

We ask that nobody lifts more than 25 pounds on their own.

## Roles

You may be asked to do any of these:

- Sort donations.
- Stock shelves.
- Pack family boxes.
- Greet clients at the door.
- Help carry boxes to cars.

Clients are neighbors. We do not ask about their income, and we do not take photos.

## Getting here

Parking is behind the building on Harbor Street. The bus stop for route 14 is across the road.

If you cannot make a shift, tell us at least 24 hours ahead by texting 555-0142, so we can find cover.

## Thank you

Last year, 312 volunteers gave 9,400 hours. Together you helped us serve 41,000 meals a month on average. Thank you.
